{% comment %}
  FUEL_06 Search & Compare designer fragrance finder.

  Renders the homepage entry band and the finder dialog it opens. Both ship
  hidden: assets/fuel06-finder.css hides everything until Intelligems puts
  ab-f06-finder on the html element, so this snippet can render on every
  homepage load without changing a single pixel of the page as it stands.

  It lives in a snippet rather than a section because templates/index.json is
  already at Shopify's 25 section cap and nothing new fits without removing
  client content. Same approach as the FUEL_05 home row: it is rendered from
  inside sections/feature-highlights.liquid, gated to the homepage, so it takes
  no template slot.

  Accepts:
  - section: {Object} the hosting section (required). All the copy comes from
    its settings, so a Swedish translation is a theme editor edit and not a
    deploy.
  - mode: {String} 'assets' | 'home' | 'dialog' (required). 'assets' emits the
    stylesheet and the script once per page and no markup. 'home' renders the
    entry band and the dialog. 'dialog' renders the dialog alone, for the
    product page, where the entry is the link under the buy button
    (snippets/fuel06-pdp-link.liquid, rendered from snippets/reactive-variant-selector.liquid).

  Usage:
  {% render 'fuel06-finder', section: section, mode: 'assets' %}
  {% render 'fuel06-finder', section: section, mode: 'home' %}
  {% render 'fuel06-finder', section: section, mode: 'dialog' %}

  The product page placement (2026-09-30, Korana: "a link with some decoration,
  somewhere below the CTA") is the 'dialog' mode plus the link snippet. Best
  Sellers and collection placements are not drawn in Figma and not built.

  Every amount shown by the finder comes from templates/collection.fuel06-index
  .liquid, which builds it with the theme's money filter. Nothing in this file
  or in the settings below carries a price, a discount or a saving.

  Remove this file, the assets it names, the index template and the render site
  in sections/feature-highlights.liquid with the FUEL_06 cleanup.
{% endcomment %}

{%- if mode == 'assets' -%}
  {{ 'fuel06-finder.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <script src="{{ 'fuel06-finder.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{%- elsif mode == 'home' or mode == 'dialog' -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign s = section.settings
    assign terms = s.fuel06_popular_terms | split: ','
    assign steps = s.fuel06_steps | strip | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
    assign title_id = 'fuel06-title-' | append: section.id
  -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Icons are captured once and reused, so the markup below stays readable and
    the glyphs cannot drift apart between the band and the dialog. The sparkle
    is the frame's own iconoir sparks-solid glyph (124:2184, 20 x 20, fill and
    a 1.25 stroke), traced from the design file on 2026-09-15; the FUEL_03
    sparkle it borrowed before was the outline drawing QA flagged. The check circle is
    bi:check-circle-fill and the cross fluent-mdl2:cancel, which are the two
    the frames name.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture icon_search -%}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="7" cy="7" r="5.25" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M11 11L14.5 14.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture icon_cancel -%}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M1 1L11 11M11 1L1 11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture icon_check -%}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M16 8A8 8 0 1 1 0 8a8 8 0 0 1 16 0zm-3.97-3.03a.75.75 0 0 0-1.08.022L7.477 9.417 5.384 7.323a.75.75 0 0 0-1.06 1.06L6.97 11.03a.75.75 0 0 0 1.079-.02l3.992-4.99a.75.75 0 0 0-.01-1.05z"/></svg>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture icon_sparks -%}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path transform="translate(1.668 1.672)" d="M5 10.833C9.063 10.833 10.833 9.124 10.833 5C10.833 9.124 12.592 10.833 16.667 10.833C12.592 10.833 10.833 12.592 10.833 16.667C10.833 12.592 9.063 10.833 5 10.833ZM0 3.75C2.612 3.75 3.75 2.652 3.75 0C3.75 2.652 4.881 3.75 7.5 3.75C4.881 3.75 3.75 4.881 3.75 7.5C3.75 4.881 2.612 3.75 0 3.75Z"/></svg>
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- capture icon_flask -%}
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 28" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 1L22 5V13C22 19.8 17.7 25.1 12 27C6.3 25.1 2 19.8 2 13V5L12 1Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M7.5 13.6L10.7 16.8L16.5 10.6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The band heading carries one word in green italic, which is drawn on the
    band and nowhere else. The word itself is a setting, so a translation can
    move it or drop it: empty, or a word the heading does not contain, prints
    the heading flat. Only the first occurrence is wrapped.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture band_heading -%}
    {%- assign accent = s.fuel06_heading_accent | strip -%}
    {%- if accent != blank and s.fuel06_heading contains accent -%}
      {%- assign head_parts = s.fuel06_heading | split: accent -%}
      {%- assign head_before = head_parts[0] -%}
      {%- capture head_cut -%}{{ head_before }}{{ accent }}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign head_after = s.fuel06_heading | remove_first: head_cut -%}
      {{- head_before | escape -}}
      <em class="fuel06-finder__accent">{{- accent | escape -}}</em>
      {{- head_after | escape -}}
    {%- else -%}
      {{- s.fuel06_heading | escape -}}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  <fuel06-finder
    data-f06-index="{{ routes.collections_url }}/all?view=fuel06-index"
    data-f06-cart-add="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"
    data-f06-based-on="{{ s.fuel06_based_on | escape }}"
    data-f06-inspired-prefix="{{ s.fuel06_inspired_prefix | escape }}"
    data-f06-brand-label="{{ s.fuel06_brand_label | escape }}"
    data-f06-brand-note="{{ s.fuel06_brand_note | escape }}"
    data-f06-save-label="{{ s.fuel06_save_label | escape }}"
    data-f06-less-suffix="{{ s.fuel06_less_suffix | escape }}"
    data-f06-add-label="{{ s.fuel06_add_label | escape }}"
    data-f06-note-labels="{{ s.fuel06_note_labels | escape }}"
    data-f06-ref-note="{{ s.fuel06_ref_note | escape }}"
    data-f06-reviews-noun="{{ s.fuel06_reviews_noun | escape }}"
    data-f06-remove-label="{{ s.fuel06_remove_label | escape }}"
    data-f06-empty="{{ s.fuel06_empty | escape }}"
    data-f06-cart-error="{{ s.fuel06_cart_error | escape }}">

    {%- comment -%}
      The same strings again as text. The store's translation app translates text on the
      page but not data attributes, so on the Danish, Norwegian and Finnish sites the
      script reads these and falls back to the attributes above.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div hidden data-f06-copy>
      <span data-f06-copy-key="f06BasedOn">{{ s.fuel06_based_on | escape }}</span>
      <span data-f06-copy-key="f06InspiredPrefix">{{ s.fuel06_inspired_prefix | escape }}</span>
      <span data-f06-copy-key="f06SaveLabel">{{ s.fuel06_save_label | escape }}</span>
      <span data-f06-copy-key="f06LessSuffix">{{ s.fuel06_less_suffix | escape }}</span>
      <span data-f06-copy-key="f06AddLabel">{{ s.fuel06_add_label | escape }}</span>
      {%- assign f06_note_labels = s.fuel06_note_labels | split: ',' -%}
      {%- for f06_note_label in f06_note_labels -%}
        <span data-f06-copy-note>{{ f06_note_label | strip | escape }}</span>
      {%- endfor -%}
      <span data-f06-copy-key="f06RefNote">{{ s.fuel06_ref_note | escape }}</span>
      <span data-f06-copy-key="f06RemoveLabel">{{ s.fuel06_remove_label | escape }}</span>
      <span data-f06-copy-key="f06Empty">{{ s.fuel06_empty | escape }}</span>
      <span data-f06-copy-key="f06CartError">{{ s.fuel06_cart_error | escape }}</span>
    </div>

    {%- if mode == 'home' -%}
    {%- comment -%} Entry band, Figma 124:2178. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="fuel06-finder fuel06-finder--entry" data-f06-entry>
      <div class="fuel06-finder__band">
        <div class="fuel06-finder__column">
          <h2 class="fuel06-finder__band-heading">{{ band_heading }}</h2>

          <label class="fuel06-finder__band-field">
            <span class="visually-hidden">{{ s.fuel06_search_label | escape }}</span>
            {{ icon_search }}
            <input
              class="fuel06-finder__band-input"
              type="search"
              autocomplete="off"
              placeholder="{{ s.fuel06_placeholder | escape }}"
              data-f06-entry-input
              data-f06-open>
          </label>

          <button type="button" class="fuel06-finder__cta" data-f06-open>
            {{ icon_sparks }}
            <span>{{ s.fuel06_cta | escape }}</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The dialog. Desktop is a centred 640 wide modal with a close cross,
      mobile is a bottom sheet 74px below the device top with a grab handle,
      which is how both are drawn. The cross rides along on mobile too: the
      sheet needs one control that a keyboard and a screen reader can reach,
      and the design does not draw one.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="fuel06-finder fuel06-finder--modal" data-f06-modal aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="fuel06-finder__scrim" data-f06-close></div>

      <div
        class="fuel06-finder__dialog"
        role="dialog"
        aria-modal="true"
        aria-labelledby="{{ title_id }}"
        tabindex="-1"
        data-f06-active="search"
        data-f06-dialog>
        {%- comment -%}
          Tapping the grab handle dismisses the sheet, which is what a bottom
          sheet is expected to do. It stays decorative and aria-hidden, and is
          not rendered above 750px where no bar is drawn and the header's own
          24px padding carries the top spacing.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="fuel06-finder__handle" data-f06-close aria-hidden="true"></div>

        <button type="button" class="fuel06-finder__close" data-f06-close aria-label="{{ s.fuel06_close_label | escape }}">
          {{ icon_cancel }}
        </button>

        <div class="fuel06-finder__body">
          {%- comment -%} State 1 and 2, Figma 154:49 and 154:50. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="fuel06-finder__state" data-f06-state="search">
            <div class="fuel06-finder__hd">
              <h2 class="fuel06-finder__title" id="{{ title_id }}">{{ s.fuel06_modal_title | escape }}</h2>
            </div>

            <div class="fuel06-finder__search">
              <span class="fuel06-finder__label fuel06-finder__label--field" id="{{ title_id }}-label">
                {{- s.fuel06_search_label | escape -}}
              </span>
              <div class="fuel06-finder__field">
                {{ icon_search }}
                <input
                  class="fuel06-finder__input"
                  type="search"
                  autocomplete="off"
                  aria-labelledby="{{ title_id }}-label"
                  placeholder="{{ s.fuel06_placeholder | escape }}"
                  data-f06-input>
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="fuel06-finder__clear"
                  data-f06-clear-input
                  aria-label="{{ s.fuel06_clear_label | escape }}">
                  {{ icon_cancel }}
                </button>
              </div>

              {%- comment -%}
                Desktop floats this over the chips and the how-it-works card,
                which stay on screen under it. The 390 sheet has neither while
                the shopper is typing, so the same markup runs inline in the
                sheet flow instead; both are frames, not a compromise.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="fuel06-finder__dropdown" data-f06-dropdown>
                <div class="fuel06-finder__sugg-block" data-f06-suggestions-block hidden>
                  <span class="fuel06-finder__label fuel06-finder__label--sugg">
                    {{- s.fuel06_suggestions_label | escape -}}
                  </span>
                  <ul class="fuel06-finder__list" data-f06-suggestions></ul>
                </div>

                <div class="fuel06-finder__recent-block" data-f06-recent-block hidden>
                  <div class="fuel06-finder__head">
                    <span class="fuel06-finder__label fuel06-finder__label--recent">
                      {{- s.fuel06_recent_label | escape -}}
                    </span>
                    <button type="button" class="fuel06-finder__link" data-f06-clear-recent>
                      {{- s.fuel06_clear_label | escape -}}
                    </button>
                  </div>
                  <ul class="fuel06-finder__list" data-f06-recent></ul>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            {%- if terms.size > 0 -%}
              <div class="fuel06-finder__popular">
                <span class="fuel06-finder__label fuel06-finder__label--popular">
                  {{- s.fuel06_popular_label | escape -}}
                </span>
                <ul class="fuel06-finder__chips">
                  {%- for term in terms -%}
                    {%- assign chip = term | strip -%}
                    {%- if chip != blank -%}
                      <li>
                        <button type="button" class="fuel06-finder__chip" data-f06-pick="{{ chip | escape }}">
                          {{- chip | escape -}}
                        </button>
                      </li>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if steps.size > 0 -%}
              <div class="fuel06-finder__how-wrap">
                <div class="fuel06-finder__how">
                  <span class="fuel06-finder__label">{{ s.fuel06_how_label | escape }}</span>
                  <ol class="fuel06-finder__steps">
                    {%- for step in steps -%}
                      {%- assign line = step | strip_html | strip -%}
                      {%- if line != blank -%}
                        <li class="fuel06-finder__step">
                          <span class="fuel06-finder__step-n" aria-hidden="true">{{ forloop.index }}</span>
                          <span class="fuel06-finder__step-t">{{ line | escape }}</span>
                        </li>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </ol>
                  {%- comment -%}
                    The botanical the frames hang off the card's right edge
                    (124:2228 desktop, 124:3055 mobile). Exported straight out
                    of Figma: one path, #146b32, the 40% opacity baked in.
                    Drawn over the steps the way the frame stacks it, and
                    clipped by the card, so it is inert to the pointer.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <img
                    class="fuel06-finder__how-leaf"
                    src="{{ 'fuel06-leaf.svg' | asset_url }}"
                    alt=""
                    aria-hidden="true"
                    width="143"
                    height="227">
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            State 3, Figma 154:144. Dev Mode exposes this as an animated GIF:
            340x341 in the modal, 366x366 on the sheet.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="fuel06-finder__state fuel06-finder__state--loading" data-f06-state="loading" hidden>
            <div class="fuel06-finder__hd">
              <h2 class="fuel06-finder__title">{{ s.fuel06_loading_title | escape }}</h2>
              <p class="fuel06-finder__sub">{{ s.fuel06_loading_sub | escape }}</p>
            </div>
            <picture class="fuel06-finder__loading-media">
              <source
                media="(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)"
                srcset="{{ 'fuel06-loading.png' | asset_url }}">
              <img
                class="fuel06-finder__loading-img"
                src="{{ 'fuel06-loading.gif' | asset_url }}"
                alt=""
                width="366"
                height="366"
                loading="lazy">
            </picture>
            <span class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite">{{ s.fuel06_loading_title | escape }}</span>
            {%- if s.fuel06_loading_note != blank -%}
              <div class="fuel06-finder__note-wrap">
                <p class="fuel06-finder__note">
                  {{ icon_flask }}
                  <span>{{ s.fuel06_loading_note | escape }}</span>
                </p>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>

          {%- comment -%} State 4, Figma 154:238. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="fuel06-finder__state" data-f06-state="result" hidden>
            <div class="fuel06-finder__hd">
              <h2 class="fuel06-finder__title">{{ s.fuel06_result_title | escape }}</h2>
              <p class="fuel06-finder__sub" data-f06-based-on></p>
            </div>

            {%- comment -%}
              The scent profile sits inside the card's right hand column on
              desktop and as its own block under the card on the sheet, so both
              share one wrapper and the grid moves it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="fuel06-finder__match-wrap">
              <div class="fuel06-finder__match" data-f06-match></div>

              <div class="fuel06-finder__scent" data-f06-scent-block hidden>
                <span class="fuel06-finder__label">{{ s.fuel06_scent_label | escape }}</span>
                <ul class="fuel06-finder__chips" data-f06-scent-chips></ul>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="fuel06-finder__notes-block" data-f06-notes-block hidden>
              <span class="fuel06-finder__label">{{ s.fuel06_notes_label | escape }}</span>
              <dl class="fuel06-finder__notes" data-f06-notes></dl>
            </div>

            <div class="fuel06-finder__compare" data-f06-compare hidden></div>

            <div data-f06-similar-block hidden>
              <span class="fuel06-finder__label">{{ s.fuel06_similar_label | escape }}</span>
              <ul class="fuel06-finder__similar" data-f06-similar></ul>
            </div>

            <p class="fuel06-finder__error" role="alert" data-f06-error></p>

            <div class="fuel06-finder__actions">
              <div class="fuel06-finder__buttons">
                <button type="button" class="fuel06-finder__btn fuel06-finder__btn--primary" data-f06-primary-add data-f06-add="">
                  {{- s.fuel06_add_label | escape -}}
                </button>
                <a class="fuel06-finder__btn fuel06-finder__btn--ghost" href="{{ routes.root_url }}" data-f06-view>
                  {{- s.fuel06_view_label | escape -}}
                </a>
              </div>

              <button type="button" class="fuel06-finder__again" data-f06-again>
                {{- s.fuel06_again_label | escape -}}
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%} State 5, Figma 154:332. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="fuel06-finder__state" data-f06-state="added" hidden>
            <div class="fuel06-finder__hd fuel06-finder__hd--row">
              {{ icon_check }}
              <h2 class="fuel06-finder__title">{{ s.fuel06_added_title | escape }}</h2>
            </div>

            <div class="fuel06-finder__added-row" data-f06-added-row></div>

            <div data-f06-also-block hidden>
              <span class="fuel06-finder__label">{{ s.fuel06_also_label | escape }}</span>
              <ul class="fuel06-finder__similar" data-f06-also></ul>
            </div>

            <p class="fuel06-finder__error" role="alert" data-f06-error></p>

            <div class="fuel06-finder__actions">
              <div class="fuel06-finder__buttons">
                <a class="fuel06-finder__btn fuel06-finder__btn--primary" href="{{ routes.cart_url }}">
                  {{- s.fuel06_bag_label | escape -}}
                </a>
                <button type="button" class="fuel06-finder__btn fuel06-finder__btn--ghost" data-f06-again>
                  {{- s.fuel06_keep_label | escape -}}
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            No result. The design draws no such state, so the wording is a
            setting and the layout is the plainest thing that can work. Omar
            still owes us this frame.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="fuel06-finder__state" data-f06-state="noresult" hidden>
            <div class="fuel06-finder__hd">
              <h2 class="fuel06-finder__title">{{ s.fuel06_noresult_title | escape }}</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="fuel06-finder__empty">
              <span data-f06-empty-query></span>
            </p>
            <p class="fuel06-finder__empty">{{ s.fuel06_empty | escape }}</p>
            <div class="fuel06-finder__actions">
              <div class="fuel06-finder__buttons">
                <button type="button" class="fuel06-finder__btn fuel06-finder__btn--ghost" data-f06-again>
                  {{- s.fuel06_again_label | escape -}}
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </fuel06-finder>
{%- endif -%}
